<title>ARGENTINA: Spanish gas firm to invest $400 mln in Argentina.</title>
<headline>Spanish gas firm to invest $400 mln in Argentina.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Gas Natural SDG said Monday it will invest $400 million over the next three years in Argentina to develop natural gas projects and export to nearby countries.</p>
<p>The state news agency Telam reported that company head Pedro Duran Farrell told President Carlos Menem that 70 percent of the investment will be channelled to manpower. There were no other details.</p>
<p>He added Gas Natural SDG also plans to diversify its business but it has no concrete plans yet.</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650</p>
